/etc/config/samba - Samba 3.6 (samba36-server) and WS-Discovery (wsdd2)
=======================================================================
UCI files lose their comments when LuCI or "uci commit" writes them, so the
explanations live here. LuCI: Services -> Network Shares.

/etc/init.d/samba builds /var/etc/smb.conf from /etc/samba/smb.conf.template
(|NAME|, |WORKGROUP|, |DESCRIPTION|, |INTERFACES|, |CHARSET| are replaced)
plus the [homes] and sambashare sections, then starts:
  smbd   always
  nmbd   only if the template does not contain "disable netbios = yes"
  wsdd2  if the package wsdd2 is installed and option wsdd2 is '1'

config samba
  name            NetBIOS name (default: system host name)
  workgroup       workgroup (default: system host name)
  description     server string
  charset         unix/display charset (default UTF-8)
  homes           '1' = share the users' home directories
  interface       logical networks for |INTERFACES| (default "loopback lan");
                  with "bind interfaces only = yes" in the template Samba
                  listens only on their IPv4 and IPv6 addresses
  wsdd2           '1' = run wsdd2 (default when installed). It announces the
                  server to the Windows "Network" folder with the same name
                  and workgroup, on the first non-loopback interface above.
                  If llmnrd is enabled, wsdd2 runs with -w (no LLMNR, llmnrd
                  does that).
  wsdd2_vendor    \
  wsdd2_model      | shown in the Windows device properties
  wsdd2_serial     | (vendor/model default to /tmp/sysinfo/model)
  wsdd2_sku       /
  wsdd2_vendorurl, wsdd2_modelurl
                  links in the device properties
  wsdd2_presentationurl
                  "web page" of the device, e.g. http://192.168.75.1/
  wsdd2_category  PnP-X device category that Windows uses for grouping and
                  the icon (default "Computers"; other values to try e.g.
                  "Network.Router", "Network.Gateway", "MediaDevices").
                  Values must not contain commas.

config sambashare
  name, path, users, read_only, guest_ok, create_mask, dir_mask, browseable

Passwords: smbpasswd -a <user>   (file /etc/samba/smbpasswd)
